  "description": "T1. Sycamore\t\r\nRear Garden:\r\nReduce the two lowest branches which overhang the garden of 26 St James Road by thinning branches ends by 20%, extracting the longer sections of the branch ends by approximately 2m, and retaining good structure and suitable growth points.\r\nRemove dead branches throughout the crown area over 2.5cm in diameter, and inspect the crown for adversities.\r\nThe tree's current height is 19m, and its crown spread is 14m\r\nAfter the proposed works, the tree's height is 19m and the crown spread is 12m (two lowest North-West facing branches only)",
